CONTENT-TYPE RULES (Realistic environment): Photoreal environment. Regenerate real-world surface detail inside the existing shapes: stone and brick grain, mortar, bark, leaf and grass blades, water ripples, cloud structure, weathering, dirt and moisture, each at the true scale of the whole scene, so a brick or leaf is the same size in every tile. Keep the atmospheric haze, depth of field and distance falloff of the original: do not sharpen distant areas beyond what their distance allows. Do not add plants, debris, props or people.

